{
  "book": "GEN",
  "chapter": 18,
  "resources": {
    "costumbres": {
      "c-041251d4729d8849": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-13",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "It is not certain that milk was formerly used in cooking meat, as is here seen to be the modern Bedawin custom.",
        "traduccion": {
          "resourceId": "freeman-13",
          "sourceHash": "b4d608042b71c0d157b35ad24bdd778cde33ff4f2df0fa5f4d9a729ef17e4379",
          "sourceLanguage": "en"
        }
      },
      "c-429143373f30648c": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-10",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "Where the soil is dry and dusty, and the feet shod with sandals, frequent washing of the feet becomes not only a luxury, but a necessity for comfort and health. It is as much a part of hospitality, under these circumstances, for a host to see that his guests’ feet are washed, as…",
        "traduccion": {
          "resourceId": "freeman-10",
          "sourceHash": "083b14d8bb21620b6ca2c622193199d12fc3d39aebf82852ddf584e8801a5ab0",
          "sourceLanguage": "en"
        }
      },
      "c-5012faffb4ee1dbb": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-8",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "The “door of the tent” is a fold of the lower part of the tent, which is fastened by a loop to the post nearby. It may thus be opened or closed at pleasure. For the sake of light and air, it is generally thrown back during the day. Noon is the hour of rest among the Orientals. Wh…",
        "traduccion": {
          "resourceId": "freeman-8",
          "sourceHash": "f3ef470eb418af4e2e9680001c0488fa2638f0d57748695b3ef5e916d9686298",
          "sourceLanguage": "en"
        }
      },
      "c-ad0dc319df82fc30": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-14",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "This was not the tent door referred to in verse 1, but the partition separating the women’s part of the tent from that belonging to the men. Such partitions are often seen in modern Bedawin tents. For description of these tents. See note on Solomon’s Song 1:5 (#474).",
        "traduccion": {
          "resourceId": "freeman-14",
          "sourceHash": "4020996453530df81cbb71a3d4113020ea49ceb624a2972b1a53d2645b97f6a7",
          "sourceLanguage": "en"
        }
      },
      "c-b69d62061c4a21ed": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-11",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "Palmer, while visiting the outlying districts of Sinai, found, upon the watershed of Wady el-Hebeibeh, the remains of a large and evidently ancient encampment. “The small stones which formerly served, as they do in the present day, for hearths, in many places still showed signs o…",
        "traduccion": {
          "resourceId": "freeman-11",
          "sourceHash": "80c96ba22f879f4f73f0e4433d1ad7b1263515b9e5e61fedd9ee71602e93f90a",
          "sourceLanguage": "en"
        }
      },
      "c-ba40e43f0521cbad": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-12",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "The primitive mariner in which Abraham and Sarah personally attended to the wants of their guests, finds illustration in what Dr. Shaw says of the Arab chieftains in Barbary. There the greatest prince is not ashamed to bring a lamb from the flock and kill it, while the princess,…",
        "traduccion": {
          "resourceId": "freeman-12",
          "sourceHash": "b373f9163366638e251a2a59c0aa6aed8eaec28c88280929dbad6ccc20e20b14",
          "sourceLanguage": "en"
        }
      },
      "c-e8a1948a07ca55bb": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-9",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "And when he saw them, he ran to meet them from the tent door, and bowed himself toward the ground, and said, My Lord, if now I have found favor in thy sight, pass not away, I pray thee, from thy servant.",
        "traduccion": {
          "resourceId": "freeman-9",
          "sourceHash": "727d0a25d9b8fd50fdf5005e07fe8b13d2822780283ebd7f82514ee5cfc1d070",
          "sourceLanguage": "en"
        }
      }
    },
